  "notes": "{腫|は}れる describes swelling of body parts from injury, infection, allergic reactions, or inflammation.\n\nIchidan verb.\n- Negative: {腫|は}れない\n- Polite: {腫|は}れます\n- Te-form: {腫|は}れて\n- Past: {腫|は}れた\n- Noun form: {腫|は}れ (swelling)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {目|め}が{腫|は}れる: eyes become swollen (from crying or allergy)\n- {足|あし}が{腫|は}れる: leg/foot swells\n- {赤|あか}く{腫|は}れる: to swell up red\n- {大|おお}きく{腫|は}れる: to swell up a lot\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {膨|ふく}れる: to puff up, to inflate (not medical)\n- {むくむ}: to be puffy, to have edema (water retention)",
